                REVISION OF ITS RETAIL ELECTRIC RATES                           )
                PURSUANT TO ADVICE NOTICE NO. 317                               )

                            ORDER ON CITY OF LAS CRUCES’ MOTION TO COMPEL

                    THIS MATTER comes before Keven Gedko and Nicholas Rossi, appointed hearing

            examiners, upon The City of Las Cruces’ (“CLC”) Motion for an Order Compelling El Paso

            Electric Company (“EPE”) to Provide Responses to the City’s Ninth Set of Interrogatories,

            Requests for Production of Documents, and Requests for Admissions (“CLC’s 9th Set”) and

            Ordering Expedited Responses to this Motion to Compel (“CLC Motion to Compel”). Being duly

            informed, the Hearing Examiners FIND and CONCLUDE:

                    1.      The CLC Motion to Compel requests that EPE be ordered to file complete

            responses to CLC’s 9th Set by no later than Wednesday, September 16, 2026.1

                    2.      The CLC Motion to Compel states that counsel for EPE informed counsel for CLC,

            that EPE intended to begin serving responses on September 11, 2026, with further responses on

            September 14, 2026 and September 15, 2026.2

                    3.      If EPE carries out its stated intentions, and EPE’s “further responses” include

            responses to the entirety of EPE’s 9th Set, then CLC’s request will be satisfied without Commission

            intervention.

                    4.      Regarding CLC’s assertions that discovery responses must be provided on the date

            that they are due,3 the Hearing Examiners note that CLC’s 9th Set contains what may be understood



